      "summary": "A Punnett square for the cross XHXh × XHY. Parent 1 gives the gametes XH and Xh and parent 2 gives XH and Y. The offspring genotypes are XHXH 1/4, XHXh 1/4, XHY 1/4 and XhY 1/4, in the ratio 1 : 1 : 1 : 1; the phenotypes are normal clotting (female) 1/2, normal clotting (male) 1/4 and haemophilia (male) 1/4, in the ratio 2 : 1 : 1."
